---
source: crates/lighthouse-cli/tests/it/surface.rs
expression: "printed(dir.path(), &args)"
---
List the findings that ask for review.

By default the open findings of decisions that authored `warn` or `info` and that no judgment stands for. A finding's `last seen` is the `--seen` evidence `review resolve` takes.

Usage: lighthouse review list [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --config <FILE>
          The project file; the project root is then the current directory
          
          [env: LIGHTHOUSE_CONFIG=]

      --decision <ID>
          Only the findings of these decisions: ids or globs

      --color <COLOR>
          Color of help and messages. `auto` honours NO_COLOR and CLICOLOR_FORCE
          
          [env: LIGHTHOUSE_COLOR=]
          [default: auto]
          [possible values: auto, always, never]

      --status <STATUS>
          Which findings: `open` is still reported and not suppressed

          Possible values:
          - open:       Still reported and not suppressed
          - suppressed: Kept out of reports by a judgment
          - narrowing:  Judged `notApplicable`, so the decision is too broad
          - inactive:   Of a rule the configuration no longer enables
          - resolved:   No longer reported by a complete run
          - all:        Every remembered finding
          
          [default: open]

      --all
          Also list findings that do not ask for review (errors, and judged ones)

      --limit <N>
          List at most this many findings, errors first, and say how many were left out. Default: 50 with `--format json`, all otherwise

      --detail <DETAIL>
          With `--format json`: compact groups findings by decision; full gives one record per finding with its full fingerprint and `lastSeen`

          Possible values:
          - compact: Grouped by decision, a decision's text said once
          - full:    One self-contained record per item
          
          [default: compact]

      --format <FORMAT>
          `text` for people, `json` for programs (its schema: `lighthouse schema`)

          Possible values:
          - text: The human form
          - json: One JSON document on one line
          
          [default: text]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
